00:00:00,103 --> 00:00:05,566
Progress after a Setback After a disappointing interview Jun felt that one

2
00:00:05,579 --> 00:00:10,303
failure would determine his destiny He began to brood over every awkward

3
00:00:10,316 --> 00:00:14,671
answer and dread the next opportunity A friend could not remove his

4
00:00:14,684 --> 00:00:20,263
sorrow but she could offer companionship and a realistic perspective She reminded

5
00:00:20,276 --> 00:00:25,882
him that a momentary setback did not signify permanent incapacity Jun decided

6
00:00:25,895 --> 00:00:30,500
to confront the problem in manageable steps He would rehearse a concise

7
00:00:30,513 --> 00:00:36,618
introduction identify one strength and ask for specific feedback He tried not

8
00:00:36,632 --> 00:00:42,368
to overestimate a competitor or underestimate himself When nervousness made him stammer

9
00:00:42,592 --> 00:00:47,632
he paused instead of rushing headlong into another sentence His tutor praised

10
00:00:47,645 --> 00:00:53,618
his willingness to persevere not a faultless performance Gradually his bitterness gave

11
00:00:53,632 --> 00:00:58,382
way to cautious optimism What helped him most was the realization that

12
00:00:58,395 --> 00:01:03,724
confidence could develop through action He did not suddenly become fearless nor

13
00:01:03,737 --> 00:01:09,461
did every difficulty disappear Nevertheless he learnt to treat uncertainty as something

14
00:01:09,474 --> 00:01:14,789
he could work with A steady effort supported by patient encouragement was

15
00:01:14,803 --> 00:01:17,987
more valuable than an empty assurance of instant success
